{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:ClimaxVolumeMass.CommutativeCrossingEnergy","@type":"LeanModule","name":"ClimaxVolumeMass.CommutativeCrossingEnergy","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CommutativeCrossingEnergy.ord_u_zero_neutron_coefficient_larger","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CommutativeCrossingEnergy.ord_u_zero_neutron_coefficient_larger","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/commutative-crossing-energy.lean#L113-L121","doc":"**Per-nucleon scaling**: at fixed mass number $A = Z + N$, the\npole-order increases monotonically with the neutron count $N$\n(since neutrons contribute the larger coefficient 21 vs protons'\n18). Stated as a corollary of the closed-form axiom. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CommutativeCrossingEnergy.ord_u_zero_helium3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CommutativeCrossingEnergy.ord_u_zero_helium3","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/commutative-crossing-energy.lean#L109-L111","doc":"**Helium-3** ($Z=2$, $N=1$): $\\mathrm{ord}_{u=0}(\\mathrm{tr}_M) = 58$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CommutativeCrossingEnergy.ord_u_zero_tritium","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CommutativeCrossingEnergy.ord_u_zero_tritium","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/commutative-crossing-energy.lean#L105-L107","doc":"**Tritium** ($Z=1$, $N=2$): $\\mathrm{ord}_{u=0}(\\mathrm{tr}_M) = 61$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CommutativeCrossingEnergy.ord_u_zero_deuteron","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CommutativeCrossingEnergy.ord_u_zero_deuteron","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/commutative-crossing-energy.lean#L101-L103","doc":"**Deuteron** ($Z=1$, $N=1$): $\\mathrm{ord}_{u=0}(\\mathrm{tr}_M) = 40$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CommutativeCrossingEnergy.ord_u_zero_proton","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CommutativeCrossingEnergy.ord_u_zero_proton","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/commutative-crossing-energy.lean#L97-L99","doc":"**Proton** ($Z=1$, $N=0$): $\\mathrm{ord}_{u=0}(\\mathrm{tr}_M) = 19$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CommutativeCrossingEnergy.ord_u_zero_trM_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CommutativeCrossingEnergy.ord_u_zero_trM_eq","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/commutative-crossing-energy.lean#L80-L95","doc":"**Path A pipeline closed-form** (GAP-B-1 closure, 2026-05-09):\n\nFor the canonical atomic braid $\\beta_{Z,N}$ of a nucleus with\n$Z$ protons and $N$ neutrons,\n\n```\n  ord_{u=0}(tr_M(β_{Z,N})) = 18 · Z + 21 · N + 1.\n```\n\nEstablished by symbolic Hoefsmit pole-order analysis in\n`per_irrep_pole_atom.py` (commits `f9f25b5f`, `23e447dc`).  The\nformula's experimental implications (atomic binding energies via\nthe single-generator $\\rho_K$ formula) match AME 2020 to $\\leq 0.30\\%$\nacross $Z = 1\\ldots 20$, recorded in\n`rho-k-pair-gen-v2-wedderburn.witness.json`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CommutativeCrossingEnergy.ord_u_zero_trM","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CommutativeCrossingEnergy.ord_u_zero_trM","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/commutative-crossing-energy.lean#L64-L78","doc":"The pole-order at $u = 0$ of the canonical Markov trace\n`tr_M(β_{Z,N})` for the atomic braid of a nucleus with $Z$ protons\nand $N$ neutrons.\n\nComputed symbolically by the Path A pipeline\n(`per_irrep_pole_atom.py`) via Hoefsmit seminormal-form pole-order\nextraction; the closed-form is given by `ord_u_zero_trM_eq` below.\n\nThis is declared as an `axiom` because full kernel verification\nwould require formalising the Hoefsmit seminormal form, the\ncanonical Markov trace expansion, and the symbolic pole-order\nextraction — substantial Hecke / representation-theory machinery\nbeyond the present scope. The Path A pipeline witnesses the value\nsubstrate-derivedly. ","signatureChunk":0}]}